Go tool that uploads completed runs from a local run_log database to the server.
One-shot: run it, it syncs whatever's pending, it exits

Build:

  cd sync
  go build -o aero-sync .

Usage:

  aero-sync -db PATH -server URL [-timeout DURATION]
  aero-sync -db PATH -dry-run

  -db PATH        run_log database to sync from (default: runs/twin_sim.db)
  -server URL     backend base URL, e.g. https://host:port (required
                     unless -dry-run)
  -timeout DUR    per-upload HTTP timeout (default: 60s)
  -dry-run        list pending runs and sample counts, no upload, no
                     network

Exit codes: 0 = synced (or nothing was pending), 1 = at least one run
failed or was ambiguous, 2 = usage error. Meant for a scheduler to alert
on non-zero.

Each run is uploaded once as a Parquet file (internal/parquetenc) plus a
session_name form field set to the run's local uuid -- the backend
assigns its own run_id and has no client-supplied idempotency key, so a
run whose outcome is ambiguous (network failure, timeout) is left
pending rather than retried automatically. Check the backend's /runs for
a matching session_name before resyncing one of those by hand.

Packages (internal/):

  store        reads run_log.db: pending runs, their samples, marks synced
  parquetenc   encodes a run's samples into the backend's Parquet schema
  backend      HTTP client for POST /ingest
  syncer       wires the above together, one Result per run

encode.go / view.go are go:build ignore dev tools for inspecting what a
run looks like once encoded (run with `go run encode.go` / `go run
view.go`) -- not part of the built binary. Their *.parquet output is
gitignored.
